==============================================================================
Claim under test: 'Case (a) alone [V_a(n)] would show O(1/n^2)
behavior' (ATTEMPT.md Sec 3.3)
==============================================================================
V_a(n) = (3*n + 1)/(6*n)
V_a(n) - 1/2 = 1/(6*n)
  -> this is exactly 1/(6n), i.e. Theta(1/n), NOT Theta(1/n^2).
  -> DIRECTLY CONTRADICTS the document's claim that Case(a) alone
     would show O(1/n^2) convergence to 1/2.

V_b(n) = (n + 1)/(3*n)
V_b(n) - 1/3 = 1/(3*n)  (= 1/(3n), also Theta(1/n))

==============================================================================
Exact decomposition of the OVERALL rate coefficient (-1/6) into
each case's WEIGHTED contribution to P_n^(1)(both) - 1/2
==============================================================================
(n-2)/n * V_a(n) = 1/2 - 5/(6*n) - 1/(3*n**2)
  deviation from 1/2 = -5/(6*n) - 1/(3*n**2)   [as n->infty, leading O(1/n) coefficient = -5/6]

(2/n) * V_b(n) = 2/(3*n) + 2/(3*n**2)
  this term itself = 2/(3*n) + 2/(3*n**2)   [as n->infty, leading O(1/n) coefficient = 2/3]

Sum = 1/2 - 1/(6*n) + 1/(3*n**2)
Sum - 1/2 = -1/(6*n) + 1/(3*n**2)
Leading O(1/n) coefficient of the SUM: -1/6

Confirmed: (n-2)/n*V_a(n) + 2/n*V_b(n) exactly equals the document's closed form (3n^2-n+2)/(6n^2). [sanity check]

==============================================================================
VERDICT on the Sec 3.3 causal narrative
==============================================================================
Case (a)'s weighted contribution to the O(1/n) coefficient: -5/6
Case (b)/(c)'s weighted contribution: 2/3
Sum of the two (must equal the overall document-claimed -1/6): -1/6  ==  -1/6

CONCLUSION: Case (a) alone contributes -5/6 to the O(1/n) rate, NOT ZERO/O(1/n^2) as the document's narrative claims. Case (b)/(c)'s contribution (2/3) does not simply 'produce' the O(1/n) rate on top of an O(1/n^2) Case-(a) baseline -- the two O(1/n) contributions PARTIALLY CANCEL (-5/6 + 2/3 = -1/6) to give the net -1/6. The document's explanatory claim that Case (a) alone 'would have shown' O(1/n^2) behavior is FALSE, directly contradicted by V_a(n)'s own closed form, (3n+1)/(6n) = 1/2 + 1/(6n).
